/*!
\page page_stbtofcollection StBTofCollection — Collection Documentation

\section btof_overview Overview

\ref StBTofCollection is the event-level container for all data produced by the
<b>Barrel Time-of-Flight (BTOF)</b> detector.  The BTOF is a cylindrical array
of 120 MRPC trays surrounding the STAR TPC, providing particle identification via
time-of-flight over a large mid-rapidity acceptance.

All BTOF objects written into \ref StEvent for a single collision — reconstructed hits,
raw TDC hits, and the event-wise header — reside here.
\ref StBTofPidTraits are stored on the associated track, not in this collection.

\section btof_ownership Object Ownership

- <b>mBTofHeader</b> (\ref StBTofHeader*): Owned by this collection. The pointer is
  assigned via \c setHeader() and is <b>deleted in the destructor</b>.
- <b>mBTofHits</b> (\c StSPtrVecBTofHit): An \c StSPtrVec; elements are owned and
  deleted when the vector is destroyed.
- <b>mBTofRawHits</b> (\c StSPtrVecBTofRawHit): Same ownership semantics.
- The collection itself is owned by the \c StEvent framework (\c StXRefMain /
  \c St_DataSet mechanism).

\section btof_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \ref StBTofHeader* | mBTofHeader | Event-wise BTOF header: VPD hit patterns, trigger timestamps, pVPD vertex z, T<sub>zero</sub> info. Owned and deleted by this class. |
| \c StSPtrVecBTofHit | mBTofHits | Collection of reconstructed \ref StBTofHit objects (tray 1–120, module 1–32, cell 1–6). |
| \c StSPtrVecBTofRawHit | mBTofRawHits | Collection of raw TDC \ref StBTofRawHit objects from the DAQ stream. |

\section btof_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c tofHeader() | Returns a pointer to the BTOF event header. |
| \c tofHits() | Returns a reference to the reconstructed hit collection. |
| \c tofRawHits() | Returns a reference to the raw TDC hit collection. |
| \c setHeader(StBTofHeader*) | Assigns the header pointer; collection takes ownership. |
| \c addHit(const StBTofHit*) | Appends a reconstructed hit (null-safe). |
| \c addRawHit(const StBTofRawHit*) | Appends a raw TDC hit (null-safe). |
| \c hitsPresent() const | Returns \c true if the reconstructed hit collection is non-empty. |
| \c rawHitsPresent() const | Returns \c true if the raw hit collection is non-empty. |

\section btof_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StBTofCollection* btofColl = event->btofCollection();
if (!btofColl) return;

// VPD vertex z from the header
if (btofColl->tofHeader()) {
    double vpdVz = btofColl->tofHeader()->vpdVz();
}

// Loop over reconstructed hits
if (btofColl->hitsPresent()) {
    const StSPtrVecBTofHit& hits = btofColl->tofHits();
    for (size_t i = 0; i < hits.size(); ++i) {
        StBTofHit* hit = hits[i];
        int tray   = hit->tray();    // 1-120
        int module = hit->module();  // 1-32
        int cell   = hit->cell();    // 1-6
    }
}
\endcode

\see StBTofHit, StBTofRawHit, StBTofHeader
*/
